{
  "name": "Snitcher — Reviewed Workflows + Ask",
  "description": "Grouped allowlist for Rex Server, Claude Code, Codex and Orca: GitHub, packages, model and account services, search, documentation, academic sources, plus via rules for ad-hoc signed Homebrew tools (gh, curl, node) in the Rex and Orca terminals. Standalone Antigravity CLI (agy) gets only its reviewed model and login hosts. Vibe Island gets its quota endpoints (Claude OAuth, Codex, agy) plus licensing and updates. Rex and Orca ts.net access; Rex Server, Tailscale Network Extension and local VM processes get STUN (UDP 3478), local virtual bridge UDP (192.168.64.0/24, 192.168.128.0/24) and dynamic peer UDP (1024-65535) for direct hole punching. Unmatched destinations ASK for the 7 managed identities; add the Default Deny group to turn this into an allowlist.",
